<article class="journal-card"><span class="pill">Sample article &middot; Planning</span><h2>Start with what matters to you</h2><p>Before browsing, write down the things you want from your next property: the space you need, the location that suits your routine and the features you value. Separate essentials from preferences so your search has a clear direction.</p><p>A short list of priorities can make it easier to compare different options and ask useful questions.</p></article>
<article class="journal-card"><span class="pill">Sample article &middot; Viewings</span><h2>Make the most of a property visit</h2><p>Take time to look at how a space would work for your daily life. Notice natural light, room layout, access and the surrounding area. Keep notes so you can compare your impressions after the visit.</p><p>Ask for clarification wherever listing details and what you see need more explanation.</p></article>
<article class="journal-card"><span class="pill">Sample article &middot; Projects</span><h2>Bring your questions to a project enquiry</h2><p>When a development interests you, make a list of questions about its location, layout, availability and current progress. Ask for the latest project information before deciding what to explore further.</p><a class="text-link" href="./projects.php">Explore projects &rarr;</a></article>
